          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                      %mo ≠
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \ne 1
                ; and
            %li
              %p
                whenever
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo +
                        %mi b
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a + b = 1
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
                or
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
                is
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/invertible"} invertible
          %p Here are a few equivalent ways to phrase the combined condition:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Whenever a (finite)
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/sum"} sum
                equals
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            %li
              %p Whenever a sum is invertible, at least one of the summands is invertible.
            %li
              %p Whenever a sum of products is invertible, for at least one of the summands, all of its multiplicands are invertible. (This is not entirely trivial in the noncommutative case, but it's still correct.)
            %li
              %p
                The invertible elements form an
                = succeed ":" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/anti-ideal"} anti-ideal
              %ul
                %li
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
                  is not invertible
                %li
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo +
                        %mi b
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a + b
                  is invertible, then either
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
                  is invertible or
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
                  is invertible
                %li
                  if
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mi b
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \cdot b
                  is invertible, then
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
                  is invertible and
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi b
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
                  is invertible
          %p
            The anti-ideal of invertible elements is in fact a minimal anti-ideal, so the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quotient+object"} quotient ring
            of a local ring by its anti-ideal of invertible elements is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+field"} Heyting field
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/residue+field"} residue field
            of the local ring.
          %p
            In the context of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/excluded+middle"} excluded middle
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+local+ring"} weak local ring
            is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+ring"} local ring
          %ul
            %li The sum of two non-invertible elements is non-invertible.
            %li
              The non-invertible elements form an
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ideal"} ideal
          %p
          #TrivialRingAsALocalRing.num_remark
            %h6 Remark
            %p
              In
              = succeed "," do
                %a{:href => "#LombardiQuitté2010"} LombardiQuitté2010
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 1
                      %mo ≠
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1 \neq 0
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+ring"} trivial ring
              is a local ring and constitutes the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/terminal+object"} terminal object
              in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/category"} categories
              of local rings.
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+field"} Heyting field
                is a local ring.
            %li
              %p
                Every
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kock+field"} Kock field
                is a local ring.
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
                a local ring, then the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+series+ring"} power series ring
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R[ [x] ]
                is also a local ring.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#jacobson_radical Jacobson radical
          %p
            The set of non-invertible elements in a local ring is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacobson+radical"} Jacobson radical
          %h3#KaplanskyTheorem Kaplansky’s theorem
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              %strong (Kaplansky)
              A
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+module"} projective module
              over a commutative local ring is a
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+module"} free module
          %p
            An exposition of the proof may be found
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://blog.jpolak.org/?p=363"} here
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive
            proof of a finitary weakening of Kaplansky’s theorem proceeds as follows.
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma Lemma
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              be a local ring. Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{a}
              be a finitely generated idempotent ideal in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔞
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{a} = (0)
              or
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔞
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{a} = (1)
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Consider
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{a}
              as a finitely generated
              = succeed "-module." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nakayama%27s+lemma"} Nakayama's lemma
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in A
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≡
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \equiv 1
              modulo
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{a}
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mi 𝔞
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \mathfrak{a} = 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is a local ring,
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
              is invertible or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo −
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1-x
              is invertible. In the first case it follows that
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔞
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{a} = (0)
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi 𝔞
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{a} = (1)
          .num_lemma
            %h6#lemma_2 Lemma
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              be a local ring. Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              be an idempotent matrix over
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is equivalent to a diagonal matrix with entries
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is idempotent, so are its ideals
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi i
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Lambda^i P)
              of
              = succeed "-minors:" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi i
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi P
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi i
                    %mi P
                    %mo ∘
                    %msup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi i
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi i
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi i
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi i
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\Lambda^i P) = (\Lambda^i (P \circ P)) =
                    (\Lambda^i P \circ \Lambda^i P) \subseteq (\Lambda^i P) \cdot (\Lambda^i P)
                    \\subseteq (\Lambda^i P).
            %p
              By the previous lemma, they are therefore each equal to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (0)
              or
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
              such that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi r
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Lambda^r P) = (1)
              and
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msup
                        %mi Λ
                        %mrow
                          %mi r
                          %mo +
                          %mn 1
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mn 0
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\Lambda^{r+1} P) = (0)
              = succeed "-minors" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi r
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (r+1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              are zero, and – since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              is a local ring – there exists at least one invertible
              = succeed "-minor." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              can be made into a diagonal matrix of the desired form by applying row and column transformations.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              We can even show that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is
              %em similar
              to a diagonal matrix with entries
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              and
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              are finite free. Combining bases of these subspaces, we obtain a basis of the full space; expressing
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              with respect to this basis, we obtain a diagonal matrix of the desired form.
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              be a finitely generated module over a local ring
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is projective. Then
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is finite free.
          .proof
            %p
              Fix a linear surjection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi A
                      %mi n
                    %mo →
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p : A^n \to M
              and a section
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo :
                      %mi M
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                      s : M \to
                      A^n
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo ≔
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∘
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P \coloneqq s \circ p
              is idempotent and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi M
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} M
              is isomorphic to
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi A
                        %mi n
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                      %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ker
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi P
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A^n/\operatorname{ker}(P)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              is equivalent to a diagonal matrix with entries
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
          %h2#in_geometry In geometry
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
            or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+geometry"} synthetic differential geometry
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+algebra"} commutative algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            with a unique maximal ideal. Hence the Spec of such an
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            has a unique closed point. Intuitively it can be thought of as some kind of “infinitesimal neighborhood” of a closed point.
          %p
            The spectrum of a ring
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/focal+point"} local
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Spec
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec R
            by open subsets one of the subsets is already the whole of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Spec
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Spec R
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is a local ring. This provides some justification for the name.
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topos+theory"} topos theory
            formulation of this is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+topos"} local topos
          %p
            An important example of a local ring in algebraic geometry is
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                    %mo =
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi ϵ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %msup
                      %mi ϵ
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R = k[\epsilon]/\epsilon^2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Spec
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{Spec} R
            to a scheme
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            correspond exactly to pairs
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi v
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x,v)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi v
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v
            is a (Zariski) tangent vector at
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
          %p
            Local rings are also important in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/deformation+theory"} deformation theory
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0
            to be a deformation of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi X
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X_0
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "0em", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} Spec
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \operatorname{Spec} R
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            is a local ring.
          %h2#in_weak_foundations In weak foundations
          %p
            Local rings are often more useful than fields when doing mathematics
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internally
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+category"} coherent category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+field"} discrete field
            (which is also coherent), it is satisfied by a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real-numbers+object"} real-numbers object
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+field"} Heyting field
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/apartness+relation"} apartness relation
            (like that on a Heyting field) in any local ring:
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo #
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \# y
            iff
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo −
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x - y
            is invertible. Then the local ring is a Heyting field if and only if this apartness relation is
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tight+relation"} tight
          #internal.num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              The addition and multiplication operations on a local ring
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              are strongly extensional with respect to the canonical apartness relation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo #
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \#
              defined by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo #
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \# y
              iff
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo −
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x - y
              is invertible. In this way a local ring becomes an internal
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring+object"} ring object
              in the category
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Apart
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Apart
          .proof
            %h6#proof_3 Proof
            %p
              Recall that products
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \times Y
              in the category of sets with apartness relations is the cartesian product of the underlying sets equipped with the apartness relation defined by
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo #
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x, y) \# (x', y')
              iff
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo #
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \# x'
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %em or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo #
                    %mi y
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y \# y'
              in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi Y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: X \to Y
              between sets with apartness relations is
              %em strongly extensional
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo #
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(x) \# f(y)
              implies
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo #
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \# y
            %p
              For addition, if
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo +
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo #
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                      %mi y
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x + y) \# (x' + y')
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo +
                    %mi y
                    %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} +
                    %mi y
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo −
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo −
                    %mi y
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x + y - (x' + y') = (x - x') + (y - y')
              is invertible, so
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo −
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x - x'
              or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo −
                    %mi y
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y - y'
              is invertible since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is local, whence
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo #
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x, y) # (x', y')
            %p
              For multiplication, if
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mi y
                      %mo #
                      %mi x
                      %mo ′
                      %mi y
                      %mo ′
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x y # x' y'
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mi y
                    %mo −
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
                    %mi y
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x y - x' y'
              is invertible. Write
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mi y
                      %mo −
                      %mi x
                      %mo ′
                      %mi y
                      %mo ′
                      %mo =
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo −
                      %mi x
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi y
                      %mo +
                      %mi x
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi y
                      %mo −
                      %mi y
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x y - x' y' = (x - x')y + x'(y - y')
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
              is local, either
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo −
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x - x')y
              is a unit or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi y
                    %mo −
                    %mi y
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x'(y - y')
              is a unit. From this we easily conclude
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo −
                    %mi x
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x - x'
              is a unit or
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi y
                    %mo −
                    %mi y
                    %mo ′
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y - y'
              is, whence
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo #
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi x
                      %mo ′
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                      %mo ′
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (x, y) # (x', y')
          %p
            Constructively there are also possible variants of the definition of local ring. For instance, in
            %a{:href => "#Johnstone77"} Johnstone77
            a
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+local+ring"} weak local ring
            is defined to be a ring in which the sum of any two noninvertible elements is noninvertible. The quotients of weak local rings are the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weak+Heyting+fields"} weak Heyting fields
            %em
              residue
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fields"} fields
            (nontrivial rings in which every noninvertible element is zero); this is the origin of the name “residue field” by Johnstone.
          %p
            There is also the notion of a
            = succeed "," do
              %strong
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/residually+discrete+local+ring"} residually discrete local ring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/apartness+relation"} apartness relation
            of the local ring is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/decidable+relation"} decidable relation
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+fields"} discrete fields
          %h2#local_homomorphisms Local homomorphisms
          %p
            Classically, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi R
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            are local rings with maximal ideals
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔪
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{m}
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝔫
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{n}
            respectively, then a ring
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi R
                  %mo →
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f: R \to S
            is said to be
            %em local
            if
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo ∃
                      %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mi 𝔫
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(\mathfrak{m}) = \exists_f (\mathfrak{m}) \subseteq \mathfrak{n}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔪
                    %mo ⊆
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi 𝔫
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{m} \subseteq f^{-1}(\mathfrak{n})
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complements"} complements
            and using the fact that taking
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inverse+images"} inverse images
            preserve complements, this is equivalent to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊆
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f^{-1}(S^\times) \subseteq R^\times
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R^\times
            is the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+units"} group of units
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi R
                    %mo ×
                  %mo ⊆
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi S
                    %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R^\times \subseteq f^{-1}(S^\times)
            (equivalently
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊆
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mo ×
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(R^\times) \subseteq S^\times
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is a ring homomorphism, so in brief
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            is local if
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi R
                      %mo ×
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi f
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi S
                      %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R^\times = f^{-1}(S^\times)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi r
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(r)
            is invertible (if and) only if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            is.
          %p
            In constructive settings it makes sense to take this last formulation as our notion of local homomorphism. In view of Proposition
            = succeed "," do
              %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#internal"}
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition Definition
            %p
              A
              %em local homomorphism
              between local rings is an internal ring homomorphism between their associated internal rings in the category
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Apart
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Apart
          %p
            Possible to-dos: say something about
            = succeed "-adic" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝔪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathfrak{m}
